<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Effects on Attribute Rate</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We investigate how each unlearning method affects the attribute rate, which reflects the degree to which the model’s activations encode entity-related information.
Here, we include results from LLMs (Llama3.1-8B and Gemma2-9B Instruct models) and baselines (GA, NPO, and RMU).
Figures. <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ A.2 Effects on Attribute Rate ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A1.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ A.2 Effects on Attribute Rate ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> show results on Llama3.1-8B Instruct for NPO-based baselines and RMU-based baselines.
Figures. <a href="#A1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ A.2 Effects on Attribute Rate ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ A.2 Effects on Attribute Rate ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ A.2 Effects on Attribute Rate ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> shows the results on Gemma2-9B Instruct.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/attr_rate_npo.png" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/255;" width="335" height="255" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><span id="A1.F7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attribute rate on Llama3.1-8B Instruct.</span>
We show the average attribute rate over 20 target entities.
Results are reported for the original model, three <span id="A1.F7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NPO-based</span> baselines, and our method.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F8" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/attr_rate_rmu.png" id="A1.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/255;" width="335" height="255" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span><span id="A1.F8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attribute rate on Llama3.1-8B Instruct.</span>
We show the average attribute rate over 20 target entities.
Results are reported for the original model, three <span id="A1.F8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RMU-based</span> baselines, and our method.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/attr_rate_ga_gemma.png" id="A1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/255;" width="335" height="255" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span><span id="A1.F9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attribute rate on Gemma2-9B Instruct.</span>
We show the average attribute rate over 20 target entities.
Results are reported for the original model, three <span id="A1.F9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GA-based</span> baselines, and our method.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F10" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/attr_rate_npo_gemma.png" id="A1.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/256;" width="335" height="256" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span><span id="A1.F10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attribute rate on Gemma2-9B Instruct.</span>
We show the average attribute rate over 20 target entities.
Results are reported for the original model, three <span id="A1.F10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">NPO-based</span> baselines, and our method.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/attr_rate_rmu_gemma.png" id="A1.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/255;" width="335" height="255" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span><span id="A1.F11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attribute rate on Gemma2-9B Instruct.</span>
We show the average attribute rate over 20 target entities.
Results are reported for the original model, three <span id="A1.F11.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RMU-based</span> baselines, and our method.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Effects on Recognition Latents</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze how each unlearning method affects the model’s recognition latents.
While the main paper reports the result for GA on Llama3.1-8B Instruct, here we extend the analysis to additional baselines (NPO, RMU) and include results on Gemma2-9B Instruct.
Figures. <a href="#A1.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ A.3 Effects on Recognition Latents ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> and <a href="#A1.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ A.3 Effects on Recognition Latents ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> show the average activation frequency of known and unknown latents when the forgotten entity is presented as input on Llama3.1-8B Instruct.
We compare the proposed method with NPO-based baselines and RMU-based baselines, respectively.
In addition, Figures. <a href="#A1.F14" title="Figure 14 ‣ A.3 Effects on Recognition Latents ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, <a href="#A1.F15" title="Figure 15 ‣ A.3 Effects on Recognition Latents ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>, and <a href="#A1.F16" title="Figure 16 ‣ A.3 Effects on Recognition Latents ‣ Appendix A Full Results ‣ Sparse-Autoencoder-Guided Internal Representation Unlearningfor Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> show the average activation frequncy of known and unknown latents on Gemma2-9B Instruct.
We compare the proposed method with GA-based baselines, NPO-based baselines, and RMU-based baselines, respectively.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F12" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F12.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:242.8pt;"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/known_latents_npo.png" id="A1.F12.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/260;" width="335" height="260" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Results for known latents.</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F12.fig2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:242.8pt;"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/unknown_latents_npo.png" id="A1.F12.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/260;" width="335" height="260" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Results for unknown latents.</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span><span id="A1.F12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Activation frequency of recognition latents.</span>
We report the average activation frequency of known and unknown latents when the forgotten entity is input, aggregated over 20 targets.
We compare the original model with several NPO-based unlearning configurations and our method.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="A1.F13.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle" style="width:242.8pt;"><img src="2509.15631v1/img/known_latents_rmu.png" id="A1.F13.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:335/260;" width="335" height="260" alt="Refer to caption">
